// The journal (engine/src/journal.rs): what it takes to study and master an entry on each
// page. An entry is seen when first found; each kill, catch, pick or mine counts toward
// studied and mastered. Pages without numbers are studied some other way (a codex
// instrument, a book) or only ever seen. `seen_within`: for a page of creatures, how near
// (blocks) a player must come, with nothing solid between, for one to count as found; a
// page without it finds its creatures only by what is done to them.
(
    pages: [
        // Ten kills show a monster's weak style, a hundred its drop table.
        (page: Monsters, studied: 10, mastered: 100, seen_within: 3.0),
        (page: Animals, studied: 10, mastered: 100, seen_within: 3.0),
        (page: Bosses, studied: 1, mastered: 10),
        (page: Fish, studied: 10, mastered: 100, seen_within: 3.0),
        (page: Plants, studied: 10, mastered: 100),
        (page: Ores, studied: 25, mastered: 250),
        (page: Collection, studied: 10, mastered: 100),
        (page: Biomes),
        (page: Breeds),
        (page: Places),
        (page: Sky),
        (page: Music),
        (page: Books),
        (page: Discoveries),
    ],
)
